commit a12c3761b3f50ab69e59c0972e8742558f13ba79
Author: peterc04 <pcoy400@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jun 12 10:28:17 2026 +0000

    decoder TC: M-atom-interleave the dW tile path (H3 move 1, task #13)

    P2_dW_GEMM was the post-H2 dominant phase (re-profiled fresh: 436.5 ms, 30.9% of
    summed-phase @ d=1024 B=16384). The dW = dYᵀ@X output-stationary GEMM ran one m64
    atom per work item (dectc_dw_run_tile / dectc_dw_run_tile_splitk both called the
    engine with MaxAtomsM=1, m_atoms=1) → the engine's kIL=min(1,kDecMaxIL)=1 → NO
    interleave, exactly H1's noted gap ("dW uses MaxAtomsM=1 → kIL=1, serial,
    unchanged"). The fwd/dX path already gets H1's 2-wide interleave (kAtomsM=2); the
    selftest's gemm_dw_kernel already exercises the FULL interleaved dW (MaxAtomsM=8,
    kIL=2) and test_dw_random_multistep(Nout=512→8 atoms) gates it — so the engine +
    ring smem were already validated; only the production DRIVER fed it 1 atom at a time.

    FIX (decoder header only; vit/mamba twins deferred per H1's portability note): a dW
    work item now owns a GROUP of up to kDecDwIL(=kDecMaxIL=2) consecutive m64 atoms.
    The engine runs the kDecDwIL wgmmas/k-step into INDEPENDENT fp32 fragments sharing
    ONE staged X (B-operand) tile → (1) the tensor pipe overlaps the independent MMAs;
    (2) the (HBM-bound) X-operand tile is staged once per group instead of per atom
    (kDecDwIL× less X traffic on the K=T contraction). Touched: dec_dw_groups/atoms
    helpers, dectc_dw_total_tiles (counts M-groups), dectc_dw_decode (→ m_group),
    dectc_dw_run_tile + dectc_dw_run_tile_splitk (MaxAtomsM=kDecDwIL, m_atoms=g_atoms),
    the split-K slot (kDecDwTileFloats now kDecDwIL·64·N — holds the group's rows) +
    dectc_dw_reduce_splitk + the compile-time kDecDwMaxTiles (group counts). Per-atom
    accumulation stays ASCENDING-k (k=0 overwrite, k>0 add) → bitwise-identical numerics.
    All decoder weights have EVEN m64-atom counts (3d=48, d=16, dff=64, V=99→2) → every
    group is exactly 2 atoms; the split-K partial-scratch total is unchanged (groups·
    kDecDwIL·64·N == atoms·64·N). DecTcSmem.sA (kDecAtomsPerSlot=min(kAtomsM,kDecMaxIL)=2
    A-tiles/slot) already had the room; no workspace growth.

    MEASURED (decoder_bench, single H100, vs HEAD c67cb66; profile-run phase split):
      d=1024 B=16384: 1192.90 -> 1041.11 ms/step (-12.7%), 8.31 -> 9.52 TF/s, MFU 0.84->0.96%
          P2_dW_GEMM 436.47 -> 302.60 ms (-30.7%); now P1_fwd dominant (353.7 ms), B1 2nd (242.8)
      d=128 B=16384 (production): 35.50 -> 32.86 ms/step (-7.4%), 4.40 -> 4.76 TF/s, MFU 0.45->0.48%
          P2_dW_GEMM 8.92 -> 6.94 ms (-22.2%); P1_bwd stays dominant (9.47 ms)

    GATES (all green):
      * d=1024 A/A/A x3 BIT-IDENTICAL (sha256 de94111a…) + PARITY bit-identical vs the
        pre-change c67cb66 build (tuning/_h3_dw_aaa.py: rebuilds baseline+live, compares).
      * test_decoder_tc.py 18/18 (incl. dW determinism + Nout=512 8-atom/4-group dW + the
        full-cell grad parity vs bf16-autocast oracle).
      * wiring_check --require-all: 33/33 (decoder/vit/mamba 11/11 each) after _ops rebuild.
      * tail-gate adamw/decoder (Δp 2.4e-7, m 2.2e-7/v 9.6e-7) + muon/decoder (Δp 1.4e-6,
        state 0/0): PASS, A/A/A bit-identical, after production _ops rebuild.

    tuning/decoder_bench.py: add a repeatable -D KEY=VAL compile-override knob (each set
    builds its own coexisting variant) for the hill-climb knob sweeps (e.g. split-K G).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

